  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.6: ChromaQwenEmbeddingGenerator refuses a text of more than 8192 tokens, MaxTokens, with an ArgumentException, before any text of the call is computed. It truncated a text at 32768 tokens: beyond 8192 the attention mask of the ONNX export needs more than 4 GiB, and in our tests a text of 16384 tokens used all the memory of a machine of 32 GB. The package runs on ONNX Runtime 1.28.0, not 1.24.4, on both targets, and on .NET 8 the default model too. In our tests the vectors of Qwen are those of 1.24.4, and those of SPLADE differ by up to 1.2e-4. From version 1.29 on, ONNX Runtime computes Qwen in float16 otherwise on Linux arm64, further from the vectors of Chroma Cloud. All the releases: https://github.com/ChromaDotNet/ChromaDB.Embeddings/releases.",
